CONTRIBUTING UPSTREAM

Upstream's CONTRIBUTING.md, from v0.3.9.3 on, sets the terms of a pull
request to upstream: by opening one, a contributor licenses the
contribution to Strato Doumanis under PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 and
grants him the right to use, change, license and distribute it for any
purpose, commercial ones included.

One pull request from this fork is open there: #15, opened on 2026-10-01
from the fork's main branch, and still open on 2026-11-01. A pull request
follows the branch it comes from, so whatever is pushed to the fork's main
is offered to upstream through it, the files in LICENSE-MIT-CYD's list
included. Until 2026-11-01 its head was the fork's main as of upstream's
v0.3.9.2 (4d913b5), from before upstream had a CONTRIBUTING.md, while all
of Pocket Tank was under the MIT License. On 2026-11-01 the push of the
fork's main as of upstream's v0.3.9.5 (daf18df) moved it there, after
upstream had a CONTRIBUTING.md: the port's files as they stood then, this
file and LICENSE-MIT-CYD among them, are offered to upstream through it. A
CYD file offered there stays MIT here; upstream would hold the rights
CONTRIBUTING.md names in it as well.
